    "summary": "Anthropic said Oct. 27 it acquired Mithril Medicine, a startup developing treatments for two rare forms of muscular dystrophy. Founder Cody Tranbarger, Mithril’s only full-time employee, used Claude to organize contracts, logistics and experiments across 11 external labs and delegated other parts of the business to the model. Mithril took one candidate from idea to […]\nThe post Anthropic Buys One-Person Biotech to Prove Claude Can Make Drugs appeared first on PYMNTS.com.",
